tags: chat-message-bytes

A limit of the node: the largest message that a client can send with celaut-chat.

The value is an integer in bytes. Example: 4096. The node refuses a message with more bytes.

The limit has no scope.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=chat-message-bytes
per=one client
rule=The node refuses a message with more bytes.
scope=none
unit=bytes
